From a6d6e1356fdbf5e49522feab67b9151c6c7c81ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:48:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(monitor): label off the single-source --pull verdict
 (b5c154cd, c01936be)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unify to ONE verdict. The prior revision computed the label from a SECOND
verdict ladder (lib/pr-verdict.js) hand-aligned to mirror pr-pull's — a
built-to-drift risk. Now the pr-monitor label + sticky headline read the SAME
value `forge shepherd <pr> --pull --json` emits (lib/pr-pull.js computeVerdict),
so they can never disagree with --pull.

- lib/pr-pull.js: export the canonical MERGE_VERDICTS enum + verdictLabel +
  VERDICT_LABELS (the single home of the verdict, next to computeVerdict).
- .github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml: new step gathers `--pull --json`, extracts
  `.verdict` (fail-closed UNKNOWN), feeds it to the sticky headline AND the
  label-reconcile (exactly one pr-verdict:<verdict>).
- lib/pr-monitor/render-sticky.js: headline now DISPLAYS a passed-in verdict
  (presentation only) — no verdict computation.
- scripts/pr-verdict-label.js: thin verdict-string -> label emitter using
  pr-pull's enum.
- DELETE lib/pr-verdict.js + its test (the parallel ladder).
- test/pr-pull.test.js: c01936be regression — buildPullPayload carries .verdict,
  computeVerdict only returns canonical values, verdictLabel fails closed.

Verified live: `--pull` on PR #403 -> BLOCKED-THREADS -> pr-verdict:blocked-threads.
Surface only: labels state, never merges, never resolves threads. Closes c01936be.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
